# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Source-material archive (~500 MB of lecture PDFs, PPTX, notebooks, datasets,
# model weights and a 159 MB sourses.zip). Read-only input to the book; never
# part of the published site.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Statistical Perspectives on Machine Learning Interpretability/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Canonical academic illustrations (Phase 5b).
# These are copyrighted figures from published papers. The book ships citation
# cards, not the images. A personally obtained copy may be dropped here for
# local reading, but must never be committed or redistributed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
assets/figures/canonical/*
!assets/figures/canonical/.gitkeep
!assets/figures/canonical/README.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build / QA output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NB: tools/baseline.json is deliberately NOT ignored — it is the pre-refactor
# content snapshot that `inventory.py --compare` checks every later phase against.
tools/*.report.txt
dist/
vnu.jar

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python (figure generation scripts under assets/figures/src)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Node (only ever used ad hoc for npx html-validate)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
package-lock.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS / editor cruft
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
